er <tab/>verba\n [[50.5]] <tab/>facta </p>\n<p> [[50.6]] [p. 254] <k>possessoriae</k>\n [[50.7]] Ager\n [[50.8]] Domus\n [[50.9]] Partes aedium <tab/>majores\n [[50.10]] <tab/>minores\n [[50.11]] Vectoria\n [[50.12]] Utensilia </p>\n<p> [[50.13]] [p. 258 sq.] <k>provisionum</k>\n [[50.14]] Sustenta<tab/>tionis <tab/>ordinariae\n [[50.15]] <tab/>extraordinariae\n [[50.16]] <tab/>Praeparationis alimentorum\n [[50.17]] Vestimentorum\n [[50.18]] Vasorum\n [[50.19]] Mixtorum et communium </p>\n<p> [[50.20]] [p. 263] (Relationes publicae sunt civiles, judiciales, militares, navales)\n [[50.21]] <k>relationes civiles</k>\n [[50.22]] Gradus personarum\n [[50.23]] Professiones\n [[50.24]] Societates\n [[50.25]] Jura\n [[50.26]] Contractus\n [[50.27]] Obligationes </p>\n<p> [[50.28]] [p. 270] <k>relationes judiciales</k>\n [[50.29]] Personae judiciales\n [[50.30]] Ordo processus\n [[50.31]] Crimina capitalia\n [[50.32]] Delicta minora\n [[51.1]] Poenae <tab/>capitales\n [[51.2]] <tab/>minores </p>\n<p> [[51.3]] [p. 280] <k>relationes navales</k>\n [[51.4]] Genera Navium\n [[51.5]] Partes aedificii\n [[51.6]] Partes <tab/>ad motum servientes aut quietem\n [[51.7]] <tab/>servientes ad directionem\n [[51.8]] Personae\n [[51.9]] Actiones </p>\n<p> [[51.10]] [p. 284] <k>relationes ecclesiasticae</k>\n [[51.11]] Religio\n [[51.12]] Personae Ecclesiasticae\n [[51.13]] Status respectu religionis\n [[51.14]] Cultus\n [[51.15]] Disciplina\n [[51.16]] Instituta per revelationem </p>\n<p> [[51.17]] [p. 298-304] Vocabula <Fn>[295 sq.] Omissa: 1) Tituli Honorum et officiorum; Termini Juridici, Heraldici; et similia. 2) Alterabilia pro seculi genio, locis et temporibus, vestimenta eorumque materia, ludi, potiones, cibi et confectiones, modi tonique musici, instrumenta artium. Nomina sectarum philosophiae, factionum politicarum, haeresium. Omnia tamen paraphrasi exprimi possunt.</Fn> sunt vel integralia vel particulae. Integralia sunt vel Radicalia\n[[51.18]] vel Derivationes vel Inflexiones. Radicales Termini sunt vel directi vel collaterales.\n[[51.19]] Directi qui reperiuntur per se in classibus praecedentibus; suntque vel genera summa\n[[51.20]] (quae in praecedentibus majusculis notavimus) vel differentiae et ex ipsis natae species.\n[[51.21]] Collaterales natae sunt ex directis per oppositionem vel per affinitatem. Derivata sunt\n[[51.22]] concreta, et abstracta. Utraque substantiva, adjectiva et adverbia; et quodlibet horum\n[[51.23]] neutrum activum passivum. Inflexiones ut in numero plurali. </p>\n<p> [[51.24]] [p. 304-308] Particulae sunt Grammaticae et transcendentales. Grammaticae sunt\n[[51.25]] Copula (<i>fuit</i> <i>est erit</i>), Pronomina (simplicia: <i>Ego tu ille. Hic idem quidam.</i> <i>Aliquis</i>,\n[[52.1]] <i>unusquisque, omnis. Quis quantus <Fn><i>Darüber</i>: ^&.!! <Leibniz special character: distilletur></Fn> qualis</i>), possessiva (<i>meus tuus suus</i>), reduplicativa\n[[52.2]] (<i>Egomet, tute, ipsemet</i>). Interjectiones admirationis, dubitationis, contemtus, odii amoris,\n[[52.3]] gaudii tristitiae, desiderii aversationis. Exclamationis silentii, allocutionis attentionis\n[[52.4]] praestandae, insinuationis minationis. </p>\n<p> [[52.5]] [p. 309-311] Praepositiones: <i>de</i> (<i>of</i>) <i>, cum; By, for; out of, concerning</i>; </p>\n<p> [[52.6]] <i>According</i> [<i>to</i>], <i>instead; with, without; for, against.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.7]] <i>To, at; From, off; Over, about.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.8]] <i>Into, in; Out of, without; Thorough, Beside.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.9]] <i>Sursum, supra above; Deorsum, infra below</i>; <i>Ante, post.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.10]] <i>Supra, infra; citra, trans. Intra, ex, adversus</i>, <angle bracket><i>contra.</i></angle bracket> </p>\n<p> [[52.11]] [p. 312-314] Adverbia: <i>Ita, non. Forte, certo.</i> <i>Quemadmodum, ita. Quomodo, sic</i>;\n[[52.12]] [<i>Magis, maxime; Minus, minime.</i>] </p>\n<p> [[52.13]] <i>Rather, than, yet, until, whilst, at length.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.14]] [<i>Simul, tantum; again</i>,] <i>as if; Un, Re.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.15]] <i>Almost, Scarce, Thereabouts.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.16]] [p. 314] <b>Conjunctiones</b>: <i>An, Num; Et, neque; Si, Nisi.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.17]] <i>Indeed, but; Although, Notwithstanding; Or, Either.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.18]] <i>That, least that; for, because; wherefore, therefore.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.19]] <i>Whereas, thereupon; Also, etc.; viz.; e. g.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.20]] [p. 315-318] Articuli, <i>ein, der.</i> </p>\n<p> [[52.21]] Imperativus modus consistit in petitione, persuasione, jussu. Modi secundarii applicati\n[[52.22]] ad potentiam (<i>kan, kould</i>), libertatem (<i>may, might</i>), voluntatem (<i>will, would</i>), Necessitatem\n[[52.23]] (<i>Must, shall; must, should</i>). </p>\n<p> [[52.24]] Tempora praesens praeteritum futurum. </p>\n<p> [[52.25]] [p. 320-322] Notae Transcendentales, variis rebus applicabiles significantes: Metaphoram\n[[52.26]] seu similitudinem; Genus, modum (<i>manner</i>); Rem, personam; </p>\n<p> [[52.27]] Locum, tempus; Causam, signum; Aggregatum, segregatum. </p>\n<p> [[52.28]] <i>Lamin, pinn; instrument, vessel; jugament, machin</i>; </p>\n<p> [[53.1]] <i>Sepiment, Armament; Vest, Armour; House, chamber</i>; </p>\n<p> [[53.2]] <i>Habit, Art; Officer, Artist; Mechanic, Merchant</i>; </p>\n<p> [[53.3]] <i>Ability, pronenes</i>; Inceptivum, frequentativum; Conatus, Impetus. </p>\n<p> [[53.4]] Augmentativum, deminutivum; <i>Excess, defect</i>; perfectivum, corruptivum; </p>\n<p> [[53.5]] vox, lingua; mas, foemina; infans, pars. </p>\n<p> [[53.6]] [p. 352] Numeri. </p>\n<p> [[53.7]] [p. 355 sq.] Signa: Hyphen, parenthesis, explicatio, interrogatio, admiratio, ironia. </p>\n",
  "number": "10₆.",
